WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.080
No!

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:38.670
Disappointed with Amaro's cowardly behavior,

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:44.430
Kotz made the foolish decision to take the gun to Mark II and face Rosamia's gapland on his own.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:48.590
If it wasn't for a timely rescue from Char and Camille,

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:50.930
Kotz would have ended up losing his life.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.490
Rise of darkness.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.990
I have a transmission from the relay station, sir.

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:21.220
Code system 22: You are to abandon pursuit if the enemy attempts to cross the Pacific.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:22.720
Return to Kennedy as soon as pop-

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:23.730
Enough!

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.230
They want to shoot them down from the Titan's New Guinea base.

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:30.000
I know perfectly well that the Kennedy spaceport is under their control, but I'm not sure.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.360
I'm not gonna let some Johnny-come-lately-titans get all the credit after I chase the aldumla

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.170
all the way out here.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:41.300
Major Bu-Ron, did you want to change the message in this communications capsule?

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:45.800
Yes, tell the Murasame Newtype Lab in Japan to keep an eye out for any unusual activity

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:46.740
in New Guinea.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:51.940
And Captain, the Newtype Lab uses a different encoding system, be sure you encode the message

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:52.940
properly.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.590
Yes sir.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:03:00.000
Captain Woodard, how many mobile suits can we deploy right now?

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.350
and one Oshima, sir.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.100
Send us out at once, sir.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:25.440
Be showing us the way to Hickory?

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.100
I didn't come all the way out here for the fun of it.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:39.740
You should take advantage of this foggy weather and make sure to get Camille and Lieutenant Quattro back into space.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.960
That's Karaba's responsibility.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.640
I thought you were supposed to be a pacifist.

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.640
Of course I hate war, like everyone else in the world!

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:53.080
But that's different from fighting when you have to defend yourself or your beliefs!

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.200
You must really despise me, then.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.800
Do you think I'm that insensitive?

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:04.130
Your mind and body were tired, so you've been sleeping these past seven years.

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:06.400
I think you really needed that rest.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.050
Now you just have to wake up.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:13.890
Once you do that, I'm sure things will return to the way they used to be for you.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.930
I don't know about that.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:21.440
In the past, you could do what Camille is doing right now, correct?

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:22.600
Yes, but...

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:29.860
Beltorchica, I don't need your pity.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.590
- Like I was saying before, I'm just not that insensitive.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:36.630
If a woman can get a man to do something

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:39.120
by simply treating him with loving care,

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.930
then that's exactly what she's going to do.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:43.640
Do you know why?

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.490
- It's because she's testing him.

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:47.590
- That's right, she's trying to find a man

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.710
that she feels is suitable for her.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.970
And if he's not, she'll just move on.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:54.110
She won't waste any time on sympathy.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:56.330
- You said earlier that you'd lost both your parents

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.690
during the one-year war.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.000
- I'm a war orphan, I'm the one who deserves

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.980
Sorry for being so serious.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:09.060
We'll send Camille and Lieutenant Quattro back into space.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:12.300
Remember, I might move on pretty easily.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.190
I don't mind.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:20.890
Director Hayato has requested to see you, Miss Bell-Tachica.

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:21.890
Thank you!

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:24.380
I don't like this Quattro guy at all.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:29.840
I was wondering if you might consider leaving another of your mobile suits behind.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.000
For what purpose?

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.850
Do I need a reason?

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:37.840
Sorry, but I can't leave the Mark II behind. Camille's a lot more accustomed to it.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:38.710
Then how about the Rick Diaz?

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:42.710
That model was developed by the Aeyug. I'm afraid it's out of the question.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.690
Is it because you don't trust Karaba?

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:48.190
Karaba won't be able to make any use of it.

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:49.190
I'll make them.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:54.230
The final battle between the Aeyug and the Titans will be determined in outer space.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:03.530
You should go up into space as well.

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:05.430
I'd prefer not to.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:09.200
I'm terrified by that sense of weightlessness.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:12.030
I think you're terrified you'll see Lala.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:16.940
Your reason says that once someone's gone, they're gone forever.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:20.890
But your heart says differently, and that's what scares you.

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:22.190
No.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:25.900
During a person's lifetime, there are certain things they should accomplish.

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:30.000
And doing those things is the best tribute you can offer to the loved ones you've lost.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:31.100
That's enough.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:07:00.000
This would make anyone

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:01.600
angry, never mind your father.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.040
I'm sorry. You can't take me up into space

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.040
now, can you? It's nothing that can't

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.590
be fixed. Cots! You're not

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:10.510
planning on taking it swimming again, are you?

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.150
That never crossed my mind, sir.

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:14.450
I felt that I should try to help out any way

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.970
I can. Camille,

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:17.990
bring that lift down. Sure.

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:20.760
I just received permission

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.600
from your father. You did?

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:25.380
Really? You mean I get

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:27.380
to go into space, too? But I'm not

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:28.540
gonna go easy on you.

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:30.000
Of course not.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:33.210
- That's great! - Yeah, I owe you guys.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.760
What's wrong?

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:38.610
What about my father? He's not coming with us?

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:42.770
He'll have a lot on his hands planning the resistance against the Titans here on Earth.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:43.780
I guess so.

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:47.220
And he needs to be available for your mother and your family.

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:50.140
We're approaching Hickory now.

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:53.670
Right.

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:55.380
Amaral.

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:59.250
The cloud covers thick along the coastline like always.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:03.140
No change in the Minovsky particle density.

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:06.540
We'll use the fog for cover and arrive at Hickory as scheduled.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:07.910
Yes, sir.

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:10.050
So do you think we'll even be able to see Hickory?

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:12.940
Beltotchka's pigeon should be arriving about now.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:14.980
We'll see a signal.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:32.090
Easy. There's a good bird.

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:36.870
No change in plans. Dispatching two mobile suits.

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:39.760
Light the fires along the runway and start sending up flares.

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:41.200
Sir.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:43.200
Any late changes in the plan to dock with the Argama?

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.200
No, there shouldn't be a problem.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:48.090
This shuttle's capable of making orbital adjustments.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:56.440
All these fires lit! Take up your air defense positions!

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:05.570
You called that one as well. You win again!

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:06.980
Of course.

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:13.220
Somewhere around here, they're going to try and get those pilots into space.

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:24.600
Arrive, sir. I've confirmed it twice.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:27.460
Start bringing us down.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.720
Did you want to ride in my mobile suit when we descend?

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:37.560
Sure.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:40.240
Hey, Bell Tachica!

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:45.710
Would it be alright if I went down to Hickory and Omro's Rick Diaz, Lieutenant?

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:47.200
Of course.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.180
Thanks, sir. I really appreciate it.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:51.740
It would be a great help if we could descend together.

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:53.540
I can at least watch your back.

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:56.040
Omro, is it okay if I ride down with you?

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:57.890
Sure, that'll be fine.

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:00.000
We'll follow you down, okay?

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.000
Okay?

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.300
Sure.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:05.300
See ya.

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:11.920
Forward hatch.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:15.060
Beltochka, take off when you can see the next flare.

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:16.060
Roger.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:22.050
Try to be careful with the linear floating seat support arm.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:22.910
Okay.

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:26.370
Why didn't you want to ride in the lieutenant's mobile suit?

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:30.000
I was just really happy to see that you were back behind the controls of a mobile suit.

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:34.490
I heard the Captain Bright is on the Argama, and I wanted to tell him that you were piloting again.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:41.410
Hey, did you see that flash just below us?

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.790
Sure did. Tell the mobile suits to get ready for takeoff.

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:48.250
Ah. Decrease altitude. It's time.

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:52.750
You there, Kotz? Make sure you do what Lieutenant Quattro tells you.

00:10:52.890 --> 00:10:54.070
Take care of Mom for me.

00:10:54.330 --> 00:10:58.030
You don't have to tell me that. Amuro, get Kotz onto that shuttle in one piece.

00:10:58.430 --> 00:10:58.830
Roger.

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:00.000
Lieutenant Quattro?

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.090
Look after him.

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:02.830
I think it'll be a good experience for me.

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:04.830
I'm kind of excited to be a substitute father.

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:07.640
I'm sure it'll be worth your while.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:08.640
Quatro out.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:19.290
Launch!

00:11:19.290 --> 00:11:21.490
Feeling okay?

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.330
Yeah, I'm all right.

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:36.820
It's the enemy.

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:37.750
Where?

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.830
They haven't spotted our mobile suits yet.

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:42.300
Shouldn't we tell Lieutenant Quattro about them?

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.850
Did you want to go into space? Then be quiet!

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:51.410
I can see the runway.

00:11:54.050 --> 00:11:56.560
This is a spaceport?

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:22.450
Go ahead. It looks like Amuro might have gotten lost coming down.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.840
Hyakushiki in Gundam.

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:34.190
It's taking Amuro.

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:35.560
Someone's here, sir.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:36.550
Hmm?

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:43.120
I'm Quattro Bojina. Sorry to trouble you.

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:46.640
Welcome to Hickory. Now let's hurry and get those mobile suits loaded.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:50.140
Do you think you have enough room on your shuttle for a Rick Diaz as well?

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:56.140
There's room, but the Argama's orders specified that the Ayug's new Hiyaku Shiki mobile suit must go back.

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:57.640
The Argama's orders?

00:12:57.640 --> 00:12:58.580
Yes!

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:09.020
Send, but keep us away from Hickory, right.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:14.870
It's just a matter of time.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:18.880
They haven't sent out any mobile suits, so they've already landed.

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:24.460
You okay?

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.210
I'm fine, get them!

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:34.100
- I got lucky.

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:40.430
-

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:46.530
- It's coming.

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:49.210
- Front, hang on to my knee.

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:50.610
- Where's the Odumla?

00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:54.500
- It's staying away from Hickory.

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:56.950
- What's taking them so long?

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:58.220
- Two of them are going now.

00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:00.000
- Put unmanned suits on the sleds and send them

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:06.800
as decoys you're in charge where are you going to the mobile suit deck hurry up with that gundam

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:14.120
what's the hold up it's not time to launch yet is it five minutes get that thing loaded we're

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:21.880
waiting for another person i'll go get him lieutenant quattro no matter what we have

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:26.600
to get the hiyakushiki back into space open these braces can't do that

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:38.440
Hickory's probably started the countdown by now, but Kotz is still on board with Anuril.

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:49.400
Diaz?

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:52.520
Go down!

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.140
Why haven't you landed your plane yet?

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:00.000
You still have Kotz!

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:04.100
with you what are you gonna do about them they started the countdown forget

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:09.190
about me zip it cots there's lots of time left you've got maybe four or five

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:19.700
minutes where's hickory from here below and to your left there you might need

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:25.490
this where you're going what a little gift this is the gun I was using when I

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:30.000
exchanged shots with shard during the one-year war but this must be really

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:40.400
valuable to you Amuro. Don't you want to be a pilot? I do. Amuro, have you seen Camille?

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:44.580
He's engaging the enemy. He should be okay in all of this fog. Take cots off

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:49.030
my hands. I don't want to give Hayato another reason to laugh at me. It's all

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:52.510
for nothing if we can't save the shuttle from their attack, understand? Leave it to

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:56.300
me. You have too many things to do in outer space and you can't stall here for

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:59.730
too long. We're not going anywhere without Camille.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:05.270
you're too important to the AU to leave behind lieutenant quattro make sure you

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:11.350
protect the shuttle on row now please move let's get to the cockpit hurry up or

00:16:11.350 --> 00:16:16.230
I might pull this trigger by mistake very well it seems I have no choice in

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:25.730
the matter

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:37.300
Just do as I say and send them out straight ahead and they might ram into the enemy.

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:41.390
He's got one!

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:48.370
The Yaudumla's under attack?

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:50.110
Yes, but they're holding them off.

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:51.910
These old shuttles pull a lot of G's.

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:52.790
I know.

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:55.590
Cuts. Guns won't fire with the safety on.

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:57.700
Nothing left to do but pray.

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:00.000
Make sure you take good care of that gun.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.110
T-minus three minutes!

00:17:02.110 --> 00:17:04.580
Aren't you scared?

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:05.670
No.

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:06.820
I'm a little bit scared.

00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:09.820
I'd rather be moving around than just sitting here.

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:13.200
Tachika?

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:16.720
It's your Gundam!

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:24.990
That's it!

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:28.960
In a fight like this, the Ashamar's mobility gives it the edge!

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:41.430
stay focused. Can you hear me? Amaro, isn't Katz with you? He's on his way to

00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:49.660
space. You're not gonna make it. You can stay with me until you get your next

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:54.420
chance. Roger that. Careful, this guy's dangerous. Beltachica must have headed

00:17:54.420 --> 00:18:00.000
back to the Audumla. How can he think of women at a time like this? Camille, ahead of you

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.000
Just below, use your bazooka!

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:04.530
Where is it? I can't see it!

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:05.540
Just fire!

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:11.220
Your dreams, just a little lower.

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:19.720
We're receiving the Argama's laser transmission. They're responding.

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:23.180
I have a message for Lieutenant Quatro.

00:18:23.480 --> 00:18:26.690
Carabao will put the Rick Diaz and the Gundam to good use.

00:18:27.030 --> 00:18:30.000
Roger. T-minus two minutes.

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:33.130
The Aldoomla?

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:34.020
Oh no.

00:18:34.020 --> 00:18:40.780
They must be nearing the end of the countdown, it won't be much longer.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:42.520
Camille!

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:51.030
Where are the other members of my team?

00:18:51.030 --> 00:18:52.900
Huh?

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:55.600
He cut the back.

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:58.100
Did you see that move?

00:18:58.100 --> 00:18:59.960
You should get back to the Aldoomla.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:00.700
You're in the way.

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:02.080
Retrieve her bioplane.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.910
Start your descent as soon as she's on board.

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:06.580
Then we'll head out over the ocean.

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:07.180
Right.

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:24.370
That must have been a decoy.

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:27.720
He's still coming at us.

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:50.270
Watch your back bad for Camille. He's not gonna make it. No, we won't but like us

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:56.510
He'll eventually return to space. This is dangerous. We're skimming the ground

00:19:57.030 --> 00:20:00.000
Keep pressing this guy's getting low on fuel watch

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:11.940
How could they be getting the better of me in mid-air combat?

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:39.000
Lift off!

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:05.040
Everything's just fine. Hickory's crew is fishing him out of the bay right now.

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:08.540
Is Amuro... really okay?

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:10.060
More than okay.

00:21:10.810 --> 00:21:14.280
I see. I think I may have to change my opinion of him.

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:15.880
Yeah, you may have to.

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:17.930
Amuro has woken from his sleep.

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:24.250
I certainly don't care for frightened men, but warlike men are just as bad.

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:30.000
I'd like to believe that he's a new type.

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:31.890
- Same here. - Look!

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:50.190
Tachika, there's nothing to cry about.

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:52.280
But Amuro!

00:21:52.280 --> 00:21:56.770
I'm sorry you didn't make it, Camille.

00:21:56.770 --> 00:22:00.000
No, I should be thanking you, Lieutenant Amuro Ray.

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:00.620
Wow.

00:22:00.620 --> 00:22:02.350
Hey, a message from Kai?

00:22:02.350 --> 00:22:05.250
Yes, but I'm afraid we can't relay messages anymore,

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:08.290
so we feel you'd be better off leaving the American continent.

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:11.240
Sure. Were you able to reach Luo and company in Hong Kong?

00:22:11.240 --> 00:22:12.640
We couldn't do it from here.

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:14.240
All right, we'll take care of it.

00:22:14.240 --> 00:22:15.240
Thanks for your help.

00:22:15.240 --> 00:22:16.990
It was our pleasure.

00:22:16.990 --> 00:22:18.240
It's from Kai.

00:22:18.240 --> 00:22:20.100
Huh?

00:22:20.100 --> 00:22:21.300
Should I open it?

00:22:21.300 --> 00:22:24.480
Please.

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:25.960
Space.

00:22:25.960 --> 00:22:28.640
I wonder how Fai is.

00:23:46.670 --> 00:23:52.660
suit that's departing from Japan is a new enemy. It's mysterious pilot Thor Marasame.

00:23:52.660 --> 00:24:00.000
Amaro soon realizes that Thor is unlike any enemy he's met in the past. Meanwhile he has a reunion

00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:05.040
Mirai and her children, and finds himself annoyed with Camille's fighting style.

00:24:05.320 --> 00:24:11.140
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam, Hong Kong City, you will see the tears of time.
